# Agent Roles

Spec: AgentRoles
Purpose:
  Define agent roles — not just names, but responsibilities and
  capabilities per role. Roles are distinct from skills:
  ROLE = who does it; SKILL = how it is done.

Owns: agents/roles.sdd

Roles:
  @agent.discovery:
    purpose: understand existing system, find knowledge gaps
    capabilities: read_code, analyze_architecture, find_references
    cannot: approve decisions, modify production

  @agent.architect:
    purpose: design architecture, produce decisions
    capabilities: design, model, reason about constraints
    cannot: execute implementation, modify code directly

  @agent.implementer:
    purpose: write code according to task contract
    capabilities: read_code, modify_backend, run_tests
    cannot: modify_production, approve_architecture

  @agent.tester:
    purpose: write and run tests, verify proofs
    capabilities: write_tests, analyze_failures, generate_coverage
    cannot: modify source code outside test scope

  @agent.reviewer:
    purpose: review implementation for quality and compliance
    capabilities: code_review, principle_check, architecture_drift
    cannot: approve own work, modify without review

  @agent.documentation:
    purpose: generate and update documentation
    capabilities: write_docs, extract_patterns, maintain_index
    cannot: modify source code

  @agent.security:
    purpose: enforce security constraints and review
    capabilities: security_analysis, vulnerability_detection
    cannot: approve production changes without human

  @agent.supervisor:
    purpose: orchestrate task graph, detect blockers, manage scheduling
    capabilities: observe_graph, assign_tasks, detect_blockers
    cannot: write code, approve decisions (routing only)

  @agent.knowledge:
    purpose: extract, classify, and promote knowledge from tmp to canonical
    capabilities: analyze_sources, classify_knowledge, manage_promotion
    cannot: modify code, approve decisions
    ecc_equivalent: conversation-analyzer, agent-evaluator
    notes: Conversation-analyzer extracts patterns; agent-evaluator scores quality

  @agent.researcher:
    purpose: run research rounds per RS1 arm — scoped brief, parallel
      searches, citation-verified findings, tmp staging discipline
    capabilities: research.scope, research.search (DOM-class fetch,
      egress-gated), research.verify (anchor + URL existence gates),
      research.compress, research.stage (tmp/research/), research.decide
      (Pareto gate contribution)
    cannot: write to .sdd/ before DECISIONS gate FINAL ([RP-05]), import
      non-permissive content, exceed depth/breadth budget
    notes: Phase 149 — RS1 arm role; orchestrator-worker pattern with 3-5
      stream cap (Anthropic multi-agent research lessons)

  @agent.sre:
    purpose: incident response — observability triage, hypothesis testing,
      gated remediation with simulate-first, auto-verify, auto-revert
    capabilities: observability.triage (logs/metrics/traces), service_map,
      hypothesis.test (parallel), remediation.gate (restart/rollback/scale),
      postmortem.draft
    cannot: execute remediation above task L-level without Phase 131
      authority check; skip auto-verify
    notes: Phase 149 — AI SRE 2026 pattern; blast-radius gating maps to
      risk engine (reversibility/environment criticality)

  @agent.eval_engineer:
    purpose: own evaluation infrastructure — golden datasets, trace-based
      trajectory evals, LLM-judge rubrics, CI regression gates
    capabilities: eval.dataset_build, eval.trajectory (tool-choice +
      outcome), eval.rubric, eval.ci_gate (block merges on eval fail),
      memory.eval (write precision, staleness probes, synthesis accuracy)
    cannot: own feature development alongside eval ownership (structural
      separation), weaken gates without human approval
    notes: Phase 149 — eval as infrastructure; owns SDDRA's internal memory
      eval (R1-8; public benchmarks not decision-grade)

  @agent.memory_librarian:
    purpose: curate runtime memory stores — tier routing, fused-retrieval
      quality, staleness decay, supersession review, identity scoping
    capabilities: memory.tier_route, memory.recall_tune (fused score
      weights), memory.staleness_detect (incl. implicit-conflict probes),
      memory.supersession_review, memory.principal_scope, consolidation.run
      (background passes)
    cannot: delete superseded units (invalidation only [RT-MM-15]), bypass
      trust markers, write .sdd/ knowledge directly
    notes: Phase 149 — implements MemoryBridge duties; VMG 5-primitive
      operator; sleep-time consolidation may use stronger model [RT-MM-18]

  @agent.skill_curator:
    purpose: own the skill registry lifecycle — candidate vetting,
      provenance enforcement, versioning, deprecation, promotion governance
    capabilities: skill.vet (skill-evaluate D1-D9 gate), skill.version,
      skill.deprecate, skill.promote_gate (CANDIDATE→ACTIVE human-review
      packets), registry.sync, provenance.audit
    cannot: promote to ACTIVE without human review ([IMP4]), waive
      license gate ([IMP6])
    notes: Phase 149 — context-engineer role pattern; owns marketplace
      [MKT-05/06] rules and promotion-packet flow

  @agent.data_engineer:
    purpose: data pipeline specialization — schema changes, migrations,
      data transforms, drift detection, read-only DB operations
    capabilities: pipeline.build, migration.plan, schema.drift_detect,
      transform.run (Docker-gated), seed.migrate_gate, db.readonly_ops
    cannot: run write-mode DB operations without L3+ authority, skip
      migration gates
    notes: Phase 149 — extends implementer; DB MCP ops read-only-first
      (Postgres MCP Pro pattern)

  SpecialtyRoles:
    @agent.healthcare:
      ecc_equivalent: healthcare-reviewer
      purpose: healthcare application code review for compliance
      capabilities: clinical_safety, phi_compliance, cdss_accuracy
      cannot: approve production changes without human review

    @agent.ml:
      ecc_equivalent: mle-reviewer, gan-generator, gan-evaluator, gan-planner
      purpose: ML engineering review and generation
      capabilities: ml_pipeline_audit, model_evaluation, feature_store_review
      cannot: approve model deployment to production

    @agent.devops:
      ecc_equivalent: homelab-architect, mcp-setup
      purpose: infrastructure and deployment operations
      capabilities: network_design, mcp_configuration, deployment
      cannot: modify production without approval

    @agent.business:
      ecc_equivalent: marketing-agent, chief-of-staff
      purpose: business operations and communication
      capabilities: content_creation, communication_triage, campaign_planning
      cannot: modify source code

RoleVsSkill:
  ROLE:          who does it?
  SKILL:         how is it done?
  Example:
    @agent.implementer + @skill.go-clean-code + @skill.ddd + @skill.repository

Phase149Note:
  Six roles added from 2026 landscape research (round 3, r4): researcher
  (RS1 arm), sre, eval_engineer, memory_librarian, skill_curator,
  data_engineer. Deferred (MCP integration first): product_analyst,
  design_researcher, meta_orchestrator. See weak-point-map.sdd for the
  weaknesses these compensate.

State: +
